  "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{T}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P\u2228(Q\u2227\u00ac(P\u2227\u00acQ)) & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228(\\text{F}\u2227\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2227\u00ac\\text{F})) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228(\\text{F}\u2227\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2227\\text{T})) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228(\\text{F}\u2227\u00ac\\text{T}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228(\\text{F}\u2227\\text{F}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2228\\text{\u00a0}\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{F}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P\u2228Q & \u2261\\text{F}\u2228\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{F}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P\u2228Q & \u2261\\text{F}\u2228\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.  \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P\u2228(Q\u2227\u00ac(P\u2227\u00acQ))\\,$ | $\\,P\u2228Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $P\u2228(Q\u2227\u00ac(P\u2227\u00acQ))$ is logically equivalent to $P\u2228Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{T},\\text{T},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nP\u2228(Q\u2227\u00ac(P\u2227\u00acQ))\u2261P\u2228Q.\n$$",
